module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.Singular.LocalHomology.Compact
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.Singular.LocalHomology.LivesOver
public import TauCeti.Topology.MappingSpace.Evaluation
public import TauCeti.Topology.Sphere.Suspension

/-!
# Spaces abundant with 2-spheres

Let `Q` be a space with a point `b`, and let `ev : Map(S², Q) → Q` be evaluation at the north
pole of the unit sphere `S² ⊆ ℝ³`, whose fibre over `b` is the double loop space
`Map_*(S², Q) = Ω²Q`. The constant maps form a section `σ : Q → Map(S², Q)` of `ev`
(`TauCeti.mappingSpaceEval_comp_const'`).

Barraud, Damian, Humilière and Oancea call a closed connected oriented `n`-manifold `Q`
**abundant with 2-spheres** if some class `α ∈ H_*(Map(S², Q); ℤ)` satisfies

1. `α` lives over the fundamental class: its image under the shriek map
   `j_! : H_*(Map(S², Q)) → H_{*-n}(Ω²Q)` of the inclusion of `b` is nonzero, and
2. either `deg α > n`, or `deg α = n` and `j_! α` is nonzero in `H_0(Ω²Q, pt)`

(their Definition 6.11, which is Definition 1.7 of the introduction). Such manifolds have finite
`π₁`-sensitive Hofer–Zehnder capacity of their unit codisc bundles (their Theorem 6.12, which is
Theorem H of the introduction).

This file states the condition with the localization at the fibre
`Hₖ(E) → Hₖ(E, E ∖ p⁻¹(b))` of `TauCeti.LivesOverFundamentalClass` in place of the shriek map
`j_!`, which is that localization followed by an isomorphism `Hₖ(E, E ∖ p⁻¹(b)) ≅ H_{k-n}(p⁻¹(b))`
natural in maps of fibrations (their Lemma 2.9). A space `Q` is abundant with 2-spheres at `b`
(`TauCeti.IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres`) if for some `k` there is `α ∈ Hₖ(Map(S², Q))` such that
`α - σ_* β` lives over the fundamental class for every `β ∈ Hₖ(Q)`. For a closed connected
oriented `n`-manifold and integer coefficients this is Definition 6.11 read through Lemma 2.9:

* in degree `k > n` the group `Hₖ(Q)` vanishes, so the condition is that `α` lives over the
  fundamental class (`TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_lt`);
* in degree `n` the group `Hₙ(Q)` is generated by `[Q]`, and `j_! σ_*[Q]` is the class of the
  constant sphere, the base point of `H_0(Ω²Q)`, whose multiples are the kernel of
  `H_0(Ω²Q) → H_0(Ω²Q, pt)`; so the condition is that `j_! α` is nonzero in `H_0(Ω²Q, pt)`,
  see
  `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_sub_zsmul`;
* in degree `k < n` no class lives over the fundamental class, since `H_{k-n}(Ω²Q) = 0`, matching
  the exclusion of these degrees in Definition 6.11.

The proof of Theorem 6.12 replaces the class `α` by `α' = α - σ_* ev_* α`, which still lives over
the fundamental class and satisfies `ev_* α' = 0`; this vanishing is what its application of the
cotangent criterion (their Proposition 6.7) needs. Conversely, a class `α'` with `ev_* α' = 0`
that lives over the fundamental class keeps doing so after subtracting any `σ_* β`, by naturality
of the localization along `σ` and `ev`. So abundance is exactly the existence of such a class
(`TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff_exists_homologyMap_eq_zero`).

Abundance is invariant under homeomorphisms of `Q`
(`Homeomorph.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff`) and under isomorphisms of the coefficients
(`CategoryTheory.Iso.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff`). The unit sphere `S³` is abundant with
2-spheres (`TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_sphere`, in
`TauCeti.AlgebraicTopology.Sphere.Abundant`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b`: some class of `Hₖ(Map(S², Q); R)` lives over the
  fundamental class at `b` modulo the classes of constant spheres.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres.exists_livesOverFundamentalClass`: an abundant space has a
  class living over the fundamental class.
* `TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff_exists_homologyMap_eq_zero`: abundance is the existence
  of a class living over the fundamental class with vanishing image under evaluation.
* `TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_isZero`: when `Hₖ(Q) = 0`, a
  class of degree `k` living over the fundamental class makes `Q` abundant.
* `TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_lt`: for a compact
  `n`-manifold, a class of degree `k > n` living over the fundamental class makes it abundant.
* `Homeomorph.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff`, `CategoryTheory.Iso.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff`:
  invariance under homeomorphisms of the space and isomorphisms of the coefficients.
* `TauCeti.HomologicalOrientation.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_sub_zsmul`:
  for a compact oriented `n`-manifold, a class of degree `n` makes it abundant when it
  lives over the fundamental class modulo the multiples of the class `σ_*[Q]` of constant spheres.

## References

* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, Definitions 1.7, 2.3 and 6.11,
  Lemma 2.9, Proposition 2.12 and the proof of Theorem 6.12.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe u

namespace TauCeti

section Coefficients

variable {Λ : Type u} [Ring Λ] (R : ModuleCat.{u} Λ) {Q : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Q]

/-- A space `Q` is **abundant with 2-spheres** at `b` if for some `k` there is a class
`α ∈ Hₖ(Map(S², Q); R)` such that `α - σ_* β` lives over the fundamental class at `b` for every
`β ∈ Hₖ(Q; R)`, for evaluation `Map(S², Q) → Q` at the north pole and the section `σ` by
constant maps.

For a closed connected oriented manifold and integer coefficients, this is Definition 6.11 of
Barraud–Damian–Humilière–Oancea, with the shriek map to the double loop space replaced by the
localization at the fibre (their Lemma 2.9). Equivalently, some class living over the fundamental
class has zero image under evaluation
(`TauCeti.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff_exists_homologyMap_eq_zero`). -/
def IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres (b : Q) : Prop :=
  ∃ (k : ℕ) (α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k :
      ModuleCat.{u} Λ)),
    ∀ β : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of Q)).homology R k : ModuleCat.{u} Λ),
      LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b
        (α - (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom ContinuousMap.const')) R k).hom
          β)

/-- Unfolding `IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres`: some class of `Hₖ(Map(S², Q))` lives over the
fundamental class after subtracting any class of constant spheres. -/
theorem isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff (b : Q) :
    IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b ↔
      ∃ (k : ℕ) (α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k :
          ModuleCat.{u} Λ)),
        ∀ β : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of Q)).homology R k : ModuleCat.{u} Λ),
          LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b
            (α - (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom ContinuousMap.const')) R
              k).hom β) :=
  Iff.rfl

variable {R}

/-- A space abundant with 2-spheres has a class of `Hₖ(Map(S², Q))` living over the fundamental
class: condition (i) of Definition 6.11. -/
theorem IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres.exists_livesOverFundamentalClass {b : Q}
    (h : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k :
        ModuleCat.{u} Λ)),
      LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b α := by
  obtain ⟨k, α, hα⟩ := h
  exact ⟨k, α, by simpa using hα 0⟩

variable (R)

/-- **Abundance through a class killed by evaluation.** A space is abundant with 2-spheres at `b`
exactly when some class `α ∈ Hₖ(Map(S², Q))` with `ev_* α = 0` lives over the fundamental class
at `b`. From a class `α` as in the definition, `α - σ_* ev_* α` is such a class; this is the
class used in the proof of Theorem 6.12 of Barraud–Damian–Humilière–Oancea. -/
theorem isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff_exists_homologyMap_eq_zero (b : Q) :
    IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b ↔
      ∃ (k : ℕ) (α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k :
          ModuleCat.{u} Λ)),
        (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north))) R
          k).hom α = 0 ∧ LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b α :=
  exists_congr fun k ↦ exists_forall_livesOverFundamentalClass_sub_iff R _ _
    (mappingSpaceEval_comp_const' Sphere2.north) b k

variable {R}

/-- **Abundance without constant classes.** If `Hₖ(Q; R) = 0`, a class of `Hₖ(Map(S², Q); R)`
that lives over the fundamental class at `b` makes `Q` abundant with 2-spheres at `b`: there is no
class of constant spheres to subtract. -/
theorem isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_isZero {k : ℕ}
    (hQ : IsZero ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of Q)).homology R k : ModuleCat.{u} Λ)) {b : Q}
    {α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k : ModuleCat.{u} Λ)}
    (hα : LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b α) :
    IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b := by
  have := ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.1 hQ
  refine ⟨k, α, fun β ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [Subsingleton.elim β 0, map_zero, sub_zero]
  exact hα

/-- **Classes above the dimension.** Let `Q` be a compact Hausdorff space modelled on a
finite-dimensional real normed space `E`. A class of `Hₖ(Map(S², Q))` with `k > dim E` that lives
over the fundamental class at `b` makes `Q` abundant with 2-spheres at `b`: here `Hₖ(Q) = 0`. -/
theorem isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_lt {E : Type u}
    [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [T2Space Q]
    [ChartedSpace E Q] [CompactSpace Q] {k : ℕ} (hk : Module.finrank ℝ E < k) {b : Q}
    {α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology R k : ModuleCat.{u} Λ)}
    (hα : LivesOverFundamentalClass R (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b α) :
    IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b :=
  isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_of_isZero
    (isZero_singularHomology_of_compactSpace (M := Q) R rfl hk) hα

/-- **Abundance transported along a homeomorphism.** If `Q` is abundant with 2-spheres at `b`, then
`Q'` is abundant with 2-spheres at `e b` for any homeomorphism `e : Q ≃ₜ Q'`. -/
theorem IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres.homeomorph {Q' : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Q'] (e : Q ≃ₜ Q')
    {b : Q} (h : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b) : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R (e b) := by
  obtain ⟨k, α, hα⟩ := h
  -- Composition with `e` identifies the mapping spaces over `e`.
  let Φ : C(Sphere2, Q) ≃ₜ C(Sphere2, Q') := Homeomorph.arrowCongr (.refl Sphere2) e
  have hΦ : (Φ.symm : C(C(Sphere2, Q'), C(Sphere2, Q))).comp (Φ : C(C(Sphere2, Q), _)) =
      ContinuousMap.id _ :=
    ContinuousMap.ext Φ.symm_apply_apply
  have hconst : (Φ.symm : C(C(Sphere2, Q'), C(Sphere2, Q))).comp ContinuousMap.const' =
      ContinuousMap.const'.comp (e.symm : C(Q', Q)) :=
    ContinuousMap.ext fun _ ↦ ContinuousMap.ext fun _ ↦ rfl
  have hfib : Φ.symm ⁻¹' (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north ⁻¹' {b}) ⊆
      mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north ⁻¹' {e b} :=
    fun f hf ↦ by
      simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, mappingSpaceEval_apply] at hf ⊢
      exact e.symm_apply_eq.1 hf
  refine ⟨k, (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (Φ : C(C(Sphere2, Q), _)))) R
    k).hom α, fun β ↦ LivesOverFundamentalClass.of_homologyMap R
      (Φ.symm : C(C(Sphere2, Q'), C(Sphere2, Q))) hfib ?_⟩
  -- `Φ⁻¹_*` undoes `Φ_*` and sends the constant spheres `σ_* β` to `σ_* e⁻¹_* β`.
  rw [map_sub, homologyMap_comp_homologyMap_of_comp_eq_id_apply R _ _ hΦ k,
    homologyMap_comp_homologyMap_apply, hconst, ← homologyMap_comp_homologyMap_apply]
  exact hα _

/-- **Abundance is invariant under homeomorphisms.** For a homeomorphism `e : Q ≃ₜ Q'`, the space
`Q'` is abundant with 2-spheres at `e b` exactly when `Q` is abundant with 2-spheres at `b`. -/
@[simp]
theorem _root_.Homeomorph.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff {Q' : Type u} [TopologicalSpace Q']
    (e : Q ≃ₜ Q') (b : Q) : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R (e b) ↔ IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ by simpa using h.homeomorph e.symm, fun h ↦ h.homeomorph e⟩

/-- **Abundance transported along a coefficient isomorphism.** If `Q` is abundant with 2-spheres
at `b` with coefficients `R`, it is so with coefficients `R'` for any isomorphism `R ≅ R'`. -/
theorem IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres.of_iso {R' : ModuleCat.{u} Λ} (e : R ≅ R') {b : Q}
    (h : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b) : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R' b := by
  obtain ⟨k, α, hα⟩ := h
  refine ⟨k, (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).app
    (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).hom α, fun β' ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨β, rfl⟩ := (ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective
    (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).app (TopCat.of Q))).1
      inferInstance β'
  -- Changing coefficients commutes with the map induced by the constant spheres; the composites
  -- in the naturality square evaluate at `β` to the two sides of `hβ`.
  let σ : C(Q, C(Sphere2, Q)) := ContinuousMap.const'
  have hβ : (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom σ)) R' k).hom
      ((((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).app (TopCat.of Q)).hom β) =
        (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).app
          (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).hom
          ((SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom σ)) R k).hom β) :=
    (congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom β)
      (((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).naturality
        (TopCat.ofHom σ))).symm
  rw [hβ]
  -- `α - σ_* β` lives over the fundamental class, hence so does its image `c α - c (σ_* β)` under
  -- the change of coefficients `c`.
  exact (Iff.of_eq (congrArg (LivesOverFundamentalClass R' (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b)
    ((((AlgebraicTopology.singularHomologyFunctor _ k).map e.hom).app
      (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).hom.map_sub _ _))).1
    ((livesOverFundamentalClass_singularHomologyFunctor_map_app_iff R e.hom).2 (hα β))

/-- **Abundance is invariant under coefficient isomorphisms.** For an isomorphism `e : R ≅ R'`, a
space is abundant with 2-spheres at `b` with coefficients `R` exactly when it is with coefficients
`R'`. -/
theorem _root_.CategoryTheory.Iso.isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_iff {R' : ModuleCat.{u} Λ} (e : R ≅ R')
    (b : Q) : IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R b ↔ IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres R' b :=
  ⟨.of_iso e, .of_iso e.symm⟩

end Coefficients

namespace HomologicalOrientation

open AlgebraicTopology

variable {Q V : Type} [TopologicalSpace Q] [T2Space Q] [CompactSpace Q]
  [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] [FiniteDimensional ℝ V] [ChartedSpace V Q] {n : ℕ}
  (o : HomologicalOrientation Q V n) (hn : Module.finrank ℝ V = n)

include o hn in
/-- **Classes in the dimension.** Let `Q` be a compact oriented `n`-manifold. A class
`α ∈ Hₙ(Map(S², Q); ℤ)` such that `α - d • σ_*[Q]` lives over the fundamental class at `b` for
every integer `d`, where `σ_*[Q]` is the class of the constant spheres, makes `Q` abundant with
2-spheres at `b`. Read through Lemma 2.9 of Barraud–Damian–Humilière–Oancea, the hypothesis is
condition (ii) of their Definition 6.11 in degree `n`: the image of `α` in `H_0(Ω²Q, pt)` is
nonzero. -/
theorem isAbundantWithTwoSpheres_of_livesOverFundamentalClass_sub_zsmul {b : Q}
    {α : ((TopCat.toSSet.obj (TopCat.of C(Sphere2, Q))).homology (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
      n : ModuleCat.{0} ℤ)}
    (hα : ∀ d : ℤ, LivesOverFundamentalClass (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ))
      (mappingSpaceEval Sphere2.north) b
        (α - d • (SSet.homologyMap (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom ContinuousMap.const'))
          (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) n).hom (o.fundamentalClass hn))) :
    IsAbundantWithTwoSpheres (ModuleCat.of ℤ (ULift.{0} ℤ)) b :=
  ⟨n, α, (o.forall_livesOverFundamentalClass_sub_iff hn _ _
    (by rw [← ContinuousMap.coe_comp, mappingSpaceEval_comp_const', ContinuousMap.coe_id]) b
      α).2 hα⟩

end HomologicalOrientation

end TauCeti
